Greetings!

I've been going back through my function library trying to
neaten things up a bit before distributing the library. 
I'm trying to hide the subroutines that are internal only,
that are called only within other functions and not directly
by the user.

So far so good, this works nicely except when the subroutine is
called by apply(). In an effort to figure out what was going on,
I wrote a very simple function that exhibits this error.

In this example, the subroutine is defined outside the main function,
and all works properly, but subtest1.s shows up in the data directory,
which is what I'm trying to avoid.

subtest1.s <- function(x, y)
{
        y * x[[1]] + x[[2]]
}

test1.s <- function(mymatrix)
{
        v2 <- apply(mymatrix, 1, function(x, y)subtest1.s(x, y), y = 2)
        v2
}

In example 2, the first call to subtest2.s works, but the second one 
doesn't.

test2.s <- function(mymatrix)
{

subtest2.s <- function(x, y)
{
        y * x[[1]] + x[[2]]
}
        
        # This call works.
