Spyros:

There are many ways to do this. Perhaps the different replies that you get
will give you some more ideas about how to do this sort of thing. Here is
one way, but there may be better ones. My suggestion is at the end.

v1 _ rep(c("A", "B", "C"), 5) 
v2 _ 1:15
dat1 _ as.data.frame(cbind(v1,v2))

   v1 v2 
 1  A  1
 2  B  2
 3  C  3
 4  A  4
 5  B  5
 6  C  6
 7  A  7
 8  B  8
 9  C  9
10  A 10
11  B 11
12  C 12
13  A 13
14  B 14
15  C 15

I want to apply cumsum to variable v2 for each 
level of v1 and cbind it in dat1.
I write:

v3 _ sapply(split(v2, v1),cumsum)
h1 _ as.data.frame(matrix(t(v3),ncol=1,byrow=F))
dat1_ cbind(dat1,h1)
dat1

**********
First of all, use tapply instead of sapply(split...)), as it's designed for
this situation:

v3<-tapply(v2,v1,cumsum)

This gives you the lists as before. Now all you have to do is assign them to
the right rows of the frame. 
h2<-numeric(nrow(dat))
for(nm in names(v3))h2[nm==dat[,1]]<- v3[[nm]]

That's it. It could also be done with match(), using some version the apply
functions to avoid the for loop, etc., but this seems simple enough.

