>From Nick Ellis 

First, it's easier to do it if the data are sorted by the factor. So, first
sort, then find the cumulative sum, then unsort. How to find the cumulative
sum? Do a simple cumulative sum (vsum) and then subtract the partial totals
(vfirst). See example:

> dat<-data.frame(fac=rep(LETTERS[1:3],6),v=1:18)[1:16,]
> dat
   fac  v
 1   A  1
 2   B  2
 3   C  3
 4   A  4
 5   B  5
 6   C  6
 7   A  7
 8   B  8
 9   C  9
10   A 10
11   B 11
12   C 12
13   A 13
14   B 14
15   C 15
16   A 16
> ord <- order(dat$fac)
> dat.sort <- dat[ord,] # work on sorted data
> dat.sort
   fac  v
 1   A  1
 4   A  4
 7   A  7
10   A 10
13   A 13
16   A 16
 2   B  2
 5   B  5
 8   B  8
11   B 11
14   B 14
 3   C  3
 6   C  6
 9   C  9
12   C 12
15   C 15
> vcum <- cumsum(dat.sort$v)
> vfirst <-
tapply(c(0,vcum[-nrow(dat.sort)]),dat.sort$fac,"[",1)[dat.sort$fac]
> cbind(vcum,vfirst,vcum-vfirst)
  vcum vfirst
A    1      0  1
A    5      0  5
A   12      0 12
A   22      0 22
