>From  Jean V. Adams

You can order the data frame by the v1 variable, calculate the cumulative
sum using tapply(), and then cbind() the result to the ordered data frame,
like this:

dat1 <- data.frame(v1=c(rep(c("A", "B", "C"), 5), "A")), v2=1:16)
dat1ord <- dat1[order(dat1$v1), ]
h <- cbind(dat1ord, cum2=unlist(tapply(dat1ord$v2, dat1ord$v1, cumsum)))

If the original order of the data frame is important to you, you could
create a new variable of row numbers, follow the procedure above, then
reorder the resulting data frame by the original row numbers.

Hope this helps.

JVA

