You might have to consider the
units and maybe the years as random effects or at least grouping
factors. To stay with S+, you should go to Schall's algorithm available
at http://www.maths.uq.edu.au/~gks/s/reglm.html, which does not have a
very good reputation. An alternative approach would be gee models
( http://biosun1.harvard.edu/~carey/index.ssoft.html) which are more
