From brad at mail.chromagraphics.com  Mon Mar 12 22:31:51 2001
From: brad at mail.chromagraphics.com (Brad Wallet)
Date: Mon, 12 Mar 2001 14:31:51 -0800
Subject: Re: subsetting problem
In-Reply-To: <saacf27b.037@EM.AGR.CA>
References: <saacf27b.037@EM.AGR.CA>
Message-ID: <Pine.LNX.4.10.10103121424100.6467-100000@mail.chromagraphics.com>

The easiest way is as follows:

S[i] _ sum(p * exp(-alpha * D[i,]) * A) - (p * exp(-alpha * D[i,i]) * A)

A more general approach is replacing D[i,] with the following:

subset _ 1:numpatch
subset _ subset[subset != i]
S[i] _ sum(p * exp(-alpha * D[i,subset]) * A)

This would work with more complex subsetting.  It is, however, overkill
with your problem.

Brad

