From peter.flom at ndri.org  Tue Mar 13 13:33:11 2001
From: peter.flom at ndri.org (Peter Flom)
Date: Tue, 13 Mar 2001 08:33:11 -0500
Subject: DV is a proportion - Summary of responses
Message-ID: <saaddb62.071@ndri.org>

Many thanks to all who responded to my question.  I am still investigating the 
various solutions offered.  Here's a summary (and, of course, if I misrepresent 
anyone's suggestion, the fault is entirely mine):

Matthew Zack suggested Box Cox transformations, and supplied a macro to perform 
them.

Dale McLerran suggested a bootstrap regression, and also supplied a macro.

Tyson Holmes and James Pratt both suggested using a Beta distribution

Don McKenzie suggested the log(p/1-p)

Theirry de Meeus suggested quasi likelihood with a logit link and mu/1-mu as 
the variance estimate

Thanks again

