I guess I'm "somebody", since I probably made the original prediction. :)

Although we announced S-PLUS 6 for Windows back in October, the project has
been delayed. The reason for the delay is that I have asked the development
team to focus their efforts in two areas: performance and quality.  The team
has already made great strides in both areas, and I'm pleased to report that
for many applications S-PLUS 6 is faster and uses much less memory than
S-PLUS 2000, and a large number of bugs reported by customers and beta
testers are in the process of being investigated and fixed.

In early May, we will providing a Release Candidate of S-PLUS 6 to S-PLUS
customers under current maintenance.  This release (on CD only, since it's
being produced before the documentation is printed) is provided for those
customers who wish to begin using S-PLUS 6 before the final release.  I've
planned a very long Quality Assurance cycle for S-PLUS 6 (this has also
contributed to the delay), and this release comes about halfway through that
process.  That said, this will be a fully-functional release, and includes
all the new features including the Excel link and CONNECT/C++.  Of course,
we'll be accepting feedback in that period, and your feedback will allow us
to fix reported bugs in the Release Candidate or its documentation before
the final release in August.

S-PLUS is currently in beta test (and has been for several months now), and
I'd like to take this opportunity to publicly thank the beta testers -- many
of whom are on this list -- for their invaluable feedback.  We'd welcome any
dedicated individuals who'd like to join the beta test program, particularly
those with time to test the Missing Data Analysis library, the Graphlets
library, and C++ integration.  If you'd like to test these features, please
drop me an email at betazone at insightful.com and I'll forward you the details
on how to register.

Finally, I'd like to extend my thanks to all S-PLUS users on the list for
your patience in awaiting S-PLUS 6 for Windows.  I hope you'll agree with me
that when the S-PLUS 6 is finally released, the extra time spent improving
the quality will have been well worth the wait.

Sincerely,
# David Smith

