This issue is covered in the on-line support pages at
http://www.insightful.com/support/ (which have been extensively updated --
you might want to take a look if you haven't seen them in a while).

On http://www.insightful.com/support/faqgraph.html it says:

16. Whenever I create a graph in S-PLUS the background is always a very dark
red color. How can I get rid of this?

This is a classic symptom of a corrupt _prefs directory. The_prefs directory
stores user preferences such as graph colors, default options, and menu
option specifications. In order to try and resolve this problem please try
the following:

1.) With S-PLUS closed, delete your _prefs directory, the default location
is:

C:\Program Files\sp2000\users\<login name>\_prefs Note that when you delete
this directory, any user-defined menus and modified defaults will be
deleted. If you have created any user-defined menus, you will want to save
the script file that created the menu options into a safe location, or save
a backup copy of the _prefs directory you are about to delete.

When restarting S-PLUS you will receive a message:

The path found for s_proj 'C:\Program Files\sp2000\users\login name' does
not contain folders '_Data' and/or 'Prefs' for project related files.
Specify another path or accept this one and the necessary folders will be
created.

Click "OK" to create the default. Just the default _prefs will be created
for you. When you restart S-PLUS, the defaults will be restored in this
directory and graphics should no longer have the dark red background that
was previously displayed.

