From pkleiber at honlab.nmfs.hawaii.edu  Wed Mar 14 19:10:37 2001
From: pkleiber at honlab.nmfs.hawaii.edu (Pierre Kleiber)
Date: Wed, 14 Mar 2001 09:10:37 -1000
Subject: Re: Extending split?
References: <8A0708778CFFD411B2030008C75DBB3B281887@msgpacpbs1.rhq.pac.dfo-mpo.gc.ca>
Message-ID: <3AAFC22D.166A00D8@honlab.nmfs.hawaii.edu>

What I usually do in that situation is make a splitting key
that is a composite of the variables you want to split on:

>  key <- paste(dat$a,dat$b)
>  splitdat <- split(dat$c,key)

The name of each element of splitdat will then indicate the
corresponding levels of dat$a and dat$b, i.e. in your example
names(splitdat) would be a vector "1 1" "1 2" "1 3" "2 1" "2 2" and
you can get at the "a" or "b" values using
substring(names(splitdat),1,1) or substring(names(splitdat),3,3)
   Pierre

