Do you have Xi = p, or Xi=1-p, where p is a proportion/
probability.  With Xi=1-p this is a complementary log-log
distribution.  It can be motivated as an extreme value
distribution.  The idea is that failure occurs when the
first of a number of "maintenance" systems fails.

I have a short note that has the details,
that will shortly appear as an appendix to a paper in
"Postharvest Biology and Technology".  The paper is:
"Apple cultivar effects on codling moth (Lepidoptera:
Torticidae) mortality following fumigation with methyl
bromide."

