From: lin at cryptic.rch.unimelb.edu.au (Ning Li)
Date: Wed, 28 Mar 2001 13:33:30 +1000
Subject: Summary(2): how to generate the sequence
Message-ID: <5.0.0.25.2.20010328124806.00ad3490@cryptic.rch.unimelb.edu.au>

Dear lister,

Many thanks to Thomas Jagger Phd from Insightful Corporation.

He contributed one more method to create a sequential id.  

The three types of methods we have had so far are:

  1) -rep(1:n, each=k)-  

      where n=unique(id), k=# of repeated
measures each id

  2)  -as.numeric(as.factor(id))-

  3)  -match(id,unique(id))-

The argument -each- in -rep()- is usually a constant, meaning that 

method 1) works if all id were observed for the same number of 

times (no missing values in a balanced design).  The 2) and 3) 

are more general in this sense. 

Best Regards

